module lib/hf/tests/md_eri
  The checks of lib/hf/md_eri against reference data, and their helpers.

mderi_prim1_worst  @70038c9e
  why   The measurement behind the test that holds mderi_prim1 to the blocks.
  PS    the prims cases' shells
  PK    the picks: which component of each shell
  L     the highest total order of a quartet
  G     the Boys grid
  W     mderi_prim1's scratch
  F     the Boys values
  worst the largest relative gap so far
  c     the case
  atoms the case's four ghost atoms
  shells the case's four shells
  pr    the case's primitives
  B     the case's block
  nb    the second shell's component count; nd the fourth's
  PQ    the four functions of a pick
  r     the pick's row
  pw    one shell's component powers
  v     mderi_prim1's value
  ref   the block's value

  = B      the reference: the whole shell block of the case
  = v      the same integral one at a time
  = worst#2  the largest relative gap

mderi_prims_case  @6ac60665
  why   The prims reference cases are single primitives on four centers; this
        builds the packs the integral code reads from one case.
  PS      the cases' shells
  c       the case
  atoms   filled: one ghost atom per shell, with no charge
  shells  filled: one shell per function
  pr      the primitives
  off     the next AO
  row     the case's row for shell k
  l       its angular momentum

mderi_prims_fix  @9c3685d1
  why   The test compares with the more accurate value wherever the two
        references disagree.

mderi_prims_ref  @31dd2e35
  why   One place decides which reference a pick is compared with.
  FX    the replacement list
  c     the case
  k     the pick
  kind  which integral of the pick
  ref   PySCF's value

mderi_prims_worst  @1f908992
  why   The measurement behind the prims test: three integrals per pick, each
        against its reference.
  PS    the cases' shells
  PK    the picks
  RG    PySCF's $(ab|cd)$; RA its $(ab|ab)$, RC its $(cd|cd)$
  FX    the replacement list
  worst the worst relative gap so far
  nrep  how many replacement references were used
  ntest how many values were tested
  lmax  the largest l seen
  ST    the case's store of two pairs
  G     the Boys grid
  B     the block $(ab|cd)$; BA $(ab|ab)$, BC $(cd|cd)$
  ab    the pick's bra row; cd its ket column
  rg    the reference for $(ab|cd)$; ra, rc for the others

  = ST       the bra and the ket pair of the case
  = worst#2  each of the three integrals of the pick is compared with its reference, mpmath's where PySCF is off
